jobs.description:
Hands-on work, teamwork, and food production. Become a production worker in the food sector in Horst. Stable job, modern working environment, and plenty of growth opportunities!
Bij welk bedrijf ga je aan de slag als Production WorkerAs a Food Production Worker in Horst, you will work at an international family-owned company specializing in the processing and packaging of fresh food products. From a modern and temperature-controlled working environment in Horst, the team works daily on quality, efficiency, and collaboration.
Wat ga je doen als Production WorkerAs a Food Production Worker in Horst, you will work in a dynamic production environment where you are responsible for sorting, processing, and packaging food products according to set guidelines. Together with your colleagues on the production line, you ensure a smooth, efficient, and hygienic production process. You monitor product quality, identify any deviations, and actively contribute to optimizing the process.

You will work in rotating shifts: an early shift from Monday to Saturday, starting at 6:00 AM and typically finishing at 2:00 PM, with possible extension until 3:30 PM. In addition, there is a (late) day shift from Monday to Friday, starting at 12:00 PM and continuing until production is completed. During busier periods, the start time may shift to 2:00 PM.
Wat wij vragen
- Good communication skills and you speak English (Dutch or Polish is a plus);

- You are stress-resistant, enjoy working in a team, and can switch tasks quickly;

- You have no objection to working in a refrigerated environment;

- You are willing to work overtime during peak season;

- You are flexible with working hours (including working every other Saturday).

Wat wij bieden 
- Starting salary of €2,549.73 gross per month, with plenty of growth opportunities based on performance;

- A solid pension scheme as a Food Production Worker in Horst;

- Opportunity for a permanent contract with the company upon good performa

Wat ga je doen? Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:
- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).
You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 
 Waar ga je werken? You’ll be working for a company that specializes in animal feed. The company is highly automated, and the machinery is modern. The work atmosphere is open and informal, and colleagues work as a team. The temperature in the workplace can vary from cold to warm, and there are approximately 70 employees at the Ittervoort location. Over time, in addition to your own department, you’ll also help out in other departments more often as needed.
The company is easily accessible from cities such as Roermond, Weert, Venlo, Peel en Maas, Stein, and Sittard-Geleen.
 Wie ben je? - MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!
 Wat mag je verwachten? - A competitive salary, based on knowledge and experience;
- A 28% shift differential for every hour worked;
